CHECK A  linear algebra vs gcd method, on the linearized lambdas
  OK  lambda = X                            dim ker = 1  2^dim =    2   gcd-method N = 2
  OK  lambda = X^2 + X                      dim ker = 0  2^dim =    1   gcd-method N = 1
  OK  lambda = X^4                          dim ker = 1  2^dim =    2   gcd-method N = 2
  OK  lambda = X^4 + X                      dim ker = 0  2^dim =    1   gcd-method N = 1
  OK  lambda = X^4 + X^2                    dim ker = 0  2^dim =    1   gcd-method N = 1
  OK  lambda = X^4 + X^2 + X                dim ker = 1  2^dim =    2   gcd-method N = 2
  OK  lambda = X^8                          dim ker = 1  2^dim =    2   gcd-method N = 2
  OK  lambda = X^8 + X^4 + X^2 + X          dim ker = 0  2^dim =    1   gcd-method N = 1
  CHECK A PASSED

CHECK B  translation involution lambda(X) -> lambda(X+1)+1
  all 248 exact-degree polynomials: N(lambda) == N(lambda(X+1)+1) -> PASSED
  lambdas (over all 248, incl. linearized) with N>2: [(132, 'X^7 + X^2', 132), (161, 'X^7 + X^5 + 1', 132), (204, 'X^7 + X^6 + X^3 + X^2', 132), (251, 'X^7 + X^6 + X^5 + X^4 + X^3 + X + 1', 132)]
  involution pairing among those: [(132, 251), (161, 204), (204, 161), (251, 132)]

CHECK D  F_2-roots recomputed combinatorially over the 244 candidates
  #candidates = 244
  distribution of the F_2-part alone: {0: 62, 1: 122, 2: 60}
  full histogram from the sweep:      {0: 62, 1: 118, 2: 60, 132: 4}
    argmax  132 X^7 + X^2                                  N=132  F_2-part=1 (0 root: True, 1 root: False)
    argmax  161 X^7 + X^5 + 1                              N=132  F_2-part=1 (0 root: False, 1 root: True)
    argmax  204 X^7 + X^6 + X^3 + X^2                      N=132  F_2-part=1 (0 root: True, 1 root: False)
    argmax  251 X^7 + X^6 + X^5 + X^4 + X^3 + X + 1        N=132  F_2-part=1 (0 root: False, 1 root: True)
  candidates whose N differs from its pure-F_2 count (other than the argmax): 0  -> consistent
